#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096437 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a0610a8-fff6-5365-be0f-1f4524fbf7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Drawing Vectors Representing Displacements"}] :question/id #uuid "5987eb83-0b8c-54f9-8295-2b25c677c855" :question/math-academy-id "e-4270" :question/problem "Show on a picture the displacement vector of a ship that travels $5\\:\\textrm{km}$ on a bearing of ${30}^{\\circ}$." :question/worked-solution "We choose an arbitrary point on the plane as the starting point (tail) of the vector. The vertical line shows the north direction.\n\n![](images/60/604ccf740830c570ee87731a719165cca75d615b3a4c8861d2671ccac95aad2e.png)\n\nWe go $30^\\circ$ clockwise from the north.\n\n![](images/a3/a370f5496c824619f0adf25caa219d4460e8bc491337d756c9ea1540b4d8223e.png)\n\nThe length of the line segment represents the distance traveled by the ship (which is $5\\:\\text{km}$)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096438 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096641 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a34cc294-bcdd-5d8d-aca3-c55ffa22d5c6" :knowledge-point/title "Drawing Equal Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "b570eb3b-dc18-5f39-8cd5-9b126f6d36d6" :question/math-academy-id "e-4271" :question/problem "Consider a vector $\\textbf{a}$ and a point $O$ (shown below). Draw a vector that is equal to the vector $\\textbf{a}$ and has its tail at $O.$\n\n![](images/57/571e2d2a8ffab997a13f99973a8605c5b9b410439239a3acef5a7fd1dac939ae.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we sketch the line that is passing through $O$ and parallel to $\\textbf{a}.$\n\n![](images/1c/1c1acea46337104f17184784dfc9fecc21360112fc510ac56665565e1c800804.png)\n\nNow, we choose a point $B$ on the line, in the direction of $\\textbf{a},$ such that $OB$ equals the length of $\\textbf{a}.$\n\n![](images/09/0931711b7da5d109085f729999016f0b7c7fb7930f658a909739910c37d05ce8.png)\n\nSo, the vector $\\overrightarrow{OB}$ is equal to the vector $\\textbf{a}$ and has its tail at $O.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096484 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69934fc1-6d88-5c34-82ae-a2d79774529d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equal Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "fa99b738-088b-54d8-938c-d3bb75ae3398" :question/math-academy-id "e-5012" :question/problem "Find the pairs of equal vectors in the diagram shown below.\n\n![](images/53/536069f862ae1044f9e924714ef3e2327c17b632a1b5da336ffac30f50fcf783.png)" :question/worked-solution "Two vectors are equal if and only if they lie on parallel lines and have both the same magnitude and the same direction.\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{e}$ are parallel and have the same direction and magnitude, hence $\\mathbf{a} = \\mathbf{e}.$ Similarly, $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{d}$ are parallel and have the same direction and magnitude, hence $\\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{d}.$\n\nOn the other hand, $\\mathbf{a} \\neq \\mathbf{b}$, $\\mathbf{a} \\neq \\mathbf{c}$ and $\\mathbf{b} \\neq \\mathbf{c}$ because they are not parallel.\n\nTherefore, we get $\\mathbf{a}=\\mathbf{e}$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{d}$ only.\n\n![](images/03/03ef54909ccfcd9c8e1f85746ec5b981e6a88c1fbf1f0c6c2337b19b05c694a7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a0610a8-fff6-5365-be0f-1f4524fbf7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Drawing Vectors Representing Displacements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "827751ff-5154-5ab5-b5ce-b69ddc4cc47e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7d/7d90ee7f259bff7244af1e3709f3ea5bdbd67ec10be795b15f5526e03221a6ab.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093687} {:answer/id #uuid "8474b0e6-81c8-5a91-bbef-95b3609209e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/02/0281d5fd55d62ecd10da8415631c7d6f57d9b3a