A}=\\text{a}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69934fc1-6d88-5c34-82ae-a2d79774529d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equal Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f5bd223-0ab0-566b-8215-fb2786fffdca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$c=d$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509750} {:answer/id #uuid "28121132-16ba-52b3-ba8d-384fae3f775e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$c=b$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509770} {:answer/id #uuid "74448826-ab0e-5e1d-84bf-76df93e08912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b=d$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509933} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f423a1-fe1b-543c-a1b7-dd95b5381997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=e$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510152} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3fae05-449b-5e15-816e-070732ed9f94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=e$ and $b=d$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9f423a1-fe1b-543c-a1b7-dd95b5381997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=e$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510152} :answer-field/id #uuid "609202e1-3f43-5d6f-bee2-5fb5865a3cda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3037d01b-d141-58a2-93b6-6c510151a0e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-118255" :question/problem "![](images/35/354df2d30981b77f75d299b868b9c2a6fc5d707a4cb643152467b5e8f43ba9e7.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following is true?" :question/worked-solution "Two vectors are equal if and only if they lie on parallel lines and have both the same magnitude and the same direction.\n\nThe vectors $b$ and $d$ have opposite directions, hence, $b\\ne d.$ \n\nOn the other hand, $c\\ne b$ and $c\\ne d$ because they are not parallel.\n\nSo, the only pair of equal vectors is $a=e.$\n\n![](images/85/853590f28737bd24abc5c02907f1d1cdb67f5c46a7d10ddc86bd90a1e7435418.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096641 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a34cc294-bcdd-5d8d-aca3-c55ffa22d5c6" :knowledge-point/title "Drawing Equal Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dff178f-0654-58f8-9b3a-b87cd1d42f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5b/5b14b463f28d9c9b0a34a7d3712e43747a50a569aa4c32e9b00ca2bb0fc25f51.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094988} {:answer/id #uuid "0fa1456f-70aa-52f0-a974-2bd0d41c6621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/54/54ed3eafa4b6d225037ad9aa9ca101728c966c992fc6aa4c5f0bb234e4b34243.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094989} {:answer/id #uuid "325cedd8-4bcf-5dc9-856e-432871445ef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/85/85476cd59e2fbab52602d9a077a11dd368c841478d08d669193eb4a14ac67ebf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094990} {:answer/id #uuid "4b0d0fc7-c408-5f45-9657-85ea3da83ca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/96/9677ef05d5751581ac1bcf83147650c0c6300a06bec6e00d9a92d4542ecba604.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094991} {:answer/id #uuid "62ffcd6e-b831-5c5f-9444-37448af6c805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/72/7202ece6ec40af7c69bffba5a25f7b742068939767d84496469f6758a7ee45f6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dff178f-0654-58f8-9b3a-b87cd1d42f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5b/5b14b463f28d9c9b0a34a7d3712e43747a50a569aa4c32e9b00ca2bb0fc25f51.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094988} :answer-field/id #uuid "89625c1f-4fd9-5385-b9c5-15da06a96aac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa655c7d-ed8e-5ecc-ad36-b5f7a59608a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-20150" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b968f83df851f5b19e7073192d7d65f938440be62c60859f553b33b75c852170.png)\n\nConsider the vector $\\text{a}$ and a point $O$ shown above. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector that is equal to the vector $\\text{a}$ and has its tail at $O.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we sketch the line that is passing through $O$ and parallel to $\\text{a}.$\n\n![](images/12/12579c5ee42e21b0a312f628bda36992fc343ace38dfbc2758a2e3d6aed49124.png)\n\nNow, we choose a point $A$ on the line, in the direction of $\\text{a},$ such that $OA$ equals the length of $\\text{a}.$\n\n![](images/cd/cdda8763ddc663d090099a30731d212a076b24063c7fdfeef9c0f7d9505709e1.png)\n\nSo, $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=\\text{a}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510382 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69934fc1-6d88-5c34-82ae-a2d79774529d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equal Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b92da83-82c4-5054-b34c-13622141632a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b=e$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509742} {:answer/id #uuid "5bdf7e3c-21c1-5db0-9927-3af377d068d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :an